    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d843">

                <pb facs="0862" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1960a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1170. A note of this Government in regard to interference with neutral commerce
                    by British authorities has been sent to London, and I have asked Mr. Page to
                    mail you a copy upon its delivery to the British Government. Upon receipt of the
                    copy, please transmit it to the French Foreign Office for the information of the
                    French Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
